{"id": "EUVD-2026-103869", "enisaUuid": "f069ef51-0ccb-3878-865a-cf3bc4d33ac7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu/gfx6: fix firmware leak on teardown\n\nThe firmware requested in gfx_v6_0_init_microcode() is not released\nwhen the GFX block is torn down, leaking the firmware resources.\n\nAdd gfx_v6_0_free_microcode() and call it from gfx_v6_0_sw_fini()\nto release the PFP, ME, CE and RLC firmware.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 386e81346f95ab0be5a82c5535de932e7a456924)", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2aee72150b0ea92804f0f2799efb129f10e46e8d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a86ebf6aa8b0a845e6188daaa6f530fe67ff00e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/652f631e2e3a8d3b11ad72dd0b8e59b5183de0d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4b70c6b34912ca0b4066f56fd627d785dfbfe1fa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc172e177795c5f87bc2d71768d077e1c10633e8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2ff4-rcmq-jgcc", "CVE-2026-98784"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "046dfc0a-e85e-33b3-bbee-1fe014e6c2ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "0934c148-14ef-398b-ba32-debbaa189071", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <cc172e177795c5f87bc2d71768d077e1c10633e8"}, {"id": "18f2557a-3f40-3921-aa6c-866e7fc8e6b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.12.113"}, {"id": "32b1ca10-3cb4-3b39-9c90-db1af2550f16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "3f8694bc-627f-3354-8d81-71cdc1403394", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <7.2.10"}, {"id": "507a9540-b242-3443-b315-acc34291519b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor